-- The definition half of the second cross-IMPORT pair. See
-- ok/section-given-import-operand-call.l4, which imports this file.
--
-- Two section GIVENs, one with a TYPICALLY default and one without, and rules
-- that read them, in the shapes an importer can use as an operand: a NUMBER, a
-- BOOLEAN, a rule with an input of its own, a rule that returns a record, and a
-- rule that returns a function.
-- Discharge runs per module, so when THIS file is discharged each of them gains
-- the section GIVEN it reads as a trailing input.

DECLARE Pair HAS a IS A NUMBER
                 b IS A NUMBER

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the window` MEANS rate TIMES 10

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is big` MEANS rate GREATER THAN 2

GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`scaled` k MEANS k TIMES rate

GIVETH A Pair
`the pair` MEANS Pair rate 2

GIVETH A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER
`adder` MEANS GIVEN x YIELD x PLUS rate

§ `Unset`
    GIVEN dflt IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the unset window` MEANS dflt TIMES 10
